BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:SPEECH Peer Educator Application Now Live!
DTSTART:20260827T130000
DTEND:20261006T035500
DTSTAMP:20260913T151801Z
UID:7804794bde2c33e8bb3b050f2ae8f1@worcester-colleges
DESCRIPTION:SPEECH Peer Educators stands for Students Promoting Expression
 \, Empathy\, and Civic Harmony. This new peer educator group aims to engag
 e the Holy Cross community in constructive dialogue around important topic
 s here on campus and in our global community. Interested in leading health
 y dialogue across difference here at Holy Cross? Consider applying for thi
 s new student leadership opportunity. Application is available via this my
 HC form. If you have any questions\, please contact Michelle Bata\, Associ
 ate Dean of Student Development\, at mbata@holycross.edu or Caitlin MacNei
 l\, Associate Director of Student Involvement\, at cemacnei@holycross.edu.
  --- Event Details: https://myhc.holycross.edu/rsvp?id=2153681\n\nSource: 
 College of the Holy Cross\nEvent page: https://myhc.holycross.edu/rsvp?id=
 2153681
LOCATION:Online Event
URL:https://myhc.holycross.edu/rsvp?id=2153681
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Apply to be an RPE!
DTSTART:20260828T130000
DTEND:20260926T040000
DTSTAMP:20260913T151801Z
UID:f8c5ac383d2d2a39467734323279f4@worcester-colleges
DESCRIPTION:To Apply to be an RPE please complete the Google Form using th
 e link below: https://forms.gle/iZMdaNgiJnjaCAym6 Below is more informatio
 n about the RPE application: Thank you for your interest in becoming a par
 t of the Relationship Peer Educators (RPE). Please complete this applicati
 on by the deadline of Friday September 25th if you would like to be consid
 ered for membership. Please note that RPEs commit for a FULL YEAR and begi
 n their membership starting in January of the SPRING semester and will con
 tinue through the Fall semester of 2026. RPE applications are open to stud
 ents of all identities As a group we recognize the importance of diverse p
 erspectives on sexual violence prevention as to maintain an intersectional
  approach and invite the voices of all experiences. The Relationship Peer 
 Educators are trained to offer support\, education\, and facilitated discu
 ssion through programming on issues of sexual assault and misconduct\, con
 sent\, and other forms of interpersonal violence for the Holy Cross commun
 ity. We do this to reduce sexual violence on campus and promote a culture 
 of healthy relationship. RPEs are private resources which means that they 
 are trained to offer support with knowledge of on campus and community res
 ources\, and to make accurate referrals to appropriate sources of help for
  fellow students. TIME COMMITMENT: Applicants are required to attend ALL o
 f the following: - RPE weekly meeting on Thursdays 4-5 p.m (Starting immed
 iately after acceptance letters are sent out for the group which is around
  mid-late October. You will be joining as a general member) - Complete sel
 f paced NASPA Peer Education Certification - Virtual RPE training on Janua
 ry 11th-14th 12-4 pm - In person RPE Training on Thursday\, January 28th f
 rom 4-6:30 p.m. AND Saturday January 30th 9am-8pm. - An early return to ca
 mpus in August 2027 for training and fall Gateways programming: First time
  RPEs must complete all required training and Gateways programs in August.
  NOTE:**This may impact your ability to participate in other organizations
  that have fall early arrival requirements such as OL\, RA\, Jo Building S
 upervisor\, SPUD\, etc. - Facilitate Bystander sessions during the fall se
 mester (dates and times TBD- generally Tuesday and Wednesday evenings 7-8:
 30pm with a requirement of up to 5 sessions a semester) After your applica
 tion is reviewed\, RPEs will contact you for a short interview. Interviews
  will take place from Monday 9/28 - Friday 10/2. BENEFITS -National Certif
 ication as a Certified Peer Educator through NASPA! -Gain extensive knowle
 dge about relationship and sexual violence\, how to effectively support su
 rvivors\, how to educate others\, and how to participate in different form
 s of activism around these issues! -Develop essential professional and res
 ume-building skills in the areas of leadership\, public speaking\, goal se
 tting\, time management\, teamwork\, program planning and evaluation! -Be 
 a leader on campus! -Work with faculty\, staff\, and student organizations
  to create change on campus! QUALIFICATIONS -First Years through Juniors c
 an apply -Creativity -Energy -Positive Attitude -Dependability and reliabi
 lity -Strong interest in promoting healthy behaviors among students -Open 
 minded and nonjudgmental - Using discretion when discussing/ sharing infor
 mation - Ability to keep personal information shared with you\, private -D
 emonstrate a sincere concern for others and their well being -Good listeni
 ng and interpersonal skills -Strong communication skills in one-on-one and
  group settings -Ability to interact and present information to the Holy C
 ross Community -Commitment to role-modeling what we educate about -Must be
  in good standing with Office of Community Standards Any questions about t
 he position or application should be directed the Associate Director of Pr
 evention and Education\, Jill Kelley (jckelley@holycross.edu) --- Event De
 tails: https://myhc.holycross.edu/rsvp?id=2153758\n\nSource: College of th
 e Holy Cross\nEvent page: https://myhc.holycross.edu/rsvp?id=2153758
LOCATION:https://forms.gle/iZMdaNgiJnjaCAym6\, 1 College Street\, Worceste
 r\, MA 01610\, United States
URL:https://myhc.holycross.edu/rsvp?id=2153758
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Apply for Student Jobs with the Hospitality Team Now Until October
  31st
DTSTART:20260909T170000
DTEND:20261031T180000
DTSTAMP:20260913T151801Z
UID:b94a126a650de3fdec7e28e4a53b67@worcester-colleges
DESCRIPTION:Our campus Hospitality team needs your help so we can provide 
 you with the best service every day. As a provider of service and job oppo
 rtunities for Holy Cross students\, let me tell you what we can offer you:
  The work commitment is small (4-6 hours per week) and we provide on the j
 ob training. Most shifts fit around academic commitments and with multiple
  dining locations to choose from\, we work with you to find the best sched
 ule that's right for you. We're more than just food service - we are a str
 ongly connected community that cares about each employee. Co-workers = fri
 ends! Students work side by side with their peers\, upperclassmen and our 
 staff to make sure you feel welcomed. While there are guidelines for what 
 to wear at work\, students can come straight from class to work without ne
 eded to change into a uniform. Serving on the Hill. A big part of coming t
 o Holy Cross is our Jesuit foundation\, which calls us all to be People fo
 r and with others. Students can give back to the community by working with
  Hospitality Services. Student staff are a big part of helping us to feed 
 the community. $15.50 Per Hour + Perfect Attendance BONUS$$ BONUS: Exclusi
 ve to students who work for Hospitality Services\, student staff\, who are
  eligible\, get paid $1 for every hour worked over the course of the semes
 ter. Paid out in one lump sum at the end of the semester. APPLY NOW >>> HE
 RE >>Having an I-9 form completed with Human Resources will expedite the e
 mployment process. To view the process click HERE GOT QUESTIONS? Email: mr
 ollo@holycross.edu Email or visit our Employment Office located in Kimball
  Hall\, 1st Floor\, Room 106 Thank you for considering working with Hospit
 ality Services. We look forward to assisting you! --- Event Details: https
 ://myhc.holycross.edu/rsvp?id=2154130\n\nSource: College of the Holy Cross
 \nEvent page: https://myhc.holycross.edu/rsvp?id=2154130
LOCATION:First floor\, Kimball Hall \, United States
URL:https://myhc.holycross.edu/rsvp?id=2154130
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Take Back The Night Story Submissions
DTSTART:20260910T170000
DTEND:20261009T210000
DTSTAMP:20260913T151801Z
UID:5f6ab39db3ff5702cc7053fae0a16a@worcester-colleges
DESCRIPTION:Take Back the Night (TBTN) for the Fall 2026 semester will be 
 Tuesday\, October 20th from 7:00-9:00pm starting on the Hoval. Please fill
  out this form by Friday 10/9 to be considered for the event. If you would
  like to speak at TBTN\, read a piece (either your own submission or an ex
 isting piece)\, and/or provide a testimony\, reading\, poem\, song\, etc.
 \, please fill out this form. We appreciate your interest and will send ou
 t more information as we approach the event. Please let us know if you hav
 e any questions. Thank you. NOTE: As described in the College’s Sexual M
 isconduct Policy\, public awareness events such as “Take Back the Night
 ”\, candlelight vigils\, “survivor speak outs” and other public form
 s in which individuals disclose incidents of sexual violence\, dating or d
 omestic violence or stalking are NOT CONSIDERED notice to the College adeq
 uate to trigger an obligation to investigate. However\, such events may in
 form the College’s prevention and education efforts. Please note that di
 sclosures of sexual or relationship violence when participating in Take Ba
 ck the Night or by sharing a survivor story will NOT result in an investig
 ation by the Office of Title IX and Equal Opportunity. Should you wish to 
 report an instance of sexual or relationship violence please contact Derek
  DeBobes\, Director of Title IX and Equal Opportunity/ Title IX Coordinato
 r either via email: ddebobes@holycross.edu or phone: (508) 793-3336. You m
 ay also submit an online report by visiting https://www.holycross.edu/offi
 ce-title-ix-and-equal-opportunity and selecting reporting options. Link to
  submit: https://forms.gle/QA2ZTVHWK4Qh7bdL9 --- Event Details: https://my
 hc.holycross.edu/rsvp?id=2154161\n\nSource: College of the Holy Cross\nEve
 nt page: https://myhc.holycross.edu/rsvp?id=2154161
LOCATION:Online Event
URL:https://myhc.holycross.edu/rsvp?id=2154161
END:VEVENT
